Ultimately, it is a matter of improving health for women and men, girls and boys, improving patient empowerment and self-management of care and treatment, and empowering care recipients and increasing their confidence.Today’s health care is yesterday’s research, and today’s research is tomorrow’s standard health care treatments.The pace of change is accelerating, major medical breakthroughs have taken place in recent years.;sustainable_agriculture_production;0.7663273215293884
Several types of cancer that we were previously powerless in the face of can now be cured or treated.Advances in assistive technologies offer completely new opportunities to improve the quality and effectiveness of care services.This can make daily life easier for both care recipients and staff.;e_health;0.9910446405410767
Similarly, the application of  4        Sweden’s national life sciences strategy Ibrahim Baylan Minister for Enterprise and Innovation Matilda Ernkrans Minister for Higher Education and Research Lena Hallengren Minister for Health and Social Affairsartificial intelligence creates new opportunities for using data and digital solutions in intelligent decision support systems and diagnostics.The changes taking place also call for skills development and create the need for new health professions, such as those that combine technological and medical expertise.Attracting top talent will be vital to ensure success.;artificial_intelligence;0.7985767722129822
Sweden’s strength is collaboration between industry, academia and the public sector, through collaboration we can build a stronger society.Together with the entire life sciences sector, we will lay the foundation for continued progress – to improve the health of the population, develop our health care system and strengthen Sweden’s economic prosperity.Sweden’s national life sciences strategy       5Contents Sweden’s national life sciences strategy       6 The role of life sciences in addressing health challenges and strengthening competitiveness          6 Priority areas        11 1.;sustainable_agriculture_production;0.8889947533607483
